-          "quote": "Let $k,m,n\\ge1$ and $p\\in\\mathbb N$, let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{m+n+p}$ be open, and let $F:U\\to\\mathbb R^n$ be $C^k$. Suppose $F(a,b,\\lambda_0)=0$ and $D_yF(a,b,\\lambda_0)$ is invertible. Then there are neighbourhoods and a unique $C^k$ map $\\varphi$ solving $F(x,\\varphi(x,\\lambda),\\lambda)=0$. More precisely, on suitable open neighbourhoods $P$ of $(a,\\lambda_0)$ and $Q$ of $b$,\n\n$$F(x,y,\\lambda)=0\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad y=\\varphi(x,\\lambda),$$\n\nand\n\n$$D\\varphi(x,\\lambda)=-D_yF(x,\\varphi(x,\\lambda),\\lambda)^{-1}D_{(x,\\lambda)}F(x,\\varphi(x,\\lambda),\\lambda).$$\n\nWhen no parameter block is present, this is the ordinary $C^k$ implicit function theorem.\n\n",
